  "summary": "Fix a memory leak when spawning subprocesses on Windows by passing `std::string::data()` directly to `CreateProcessA` instead of heap-allocating a copy. This eliminates an undeleted `new[]` buffer allocation in `Popen::execute_process()`.",
  "problem": "On Windows, every invocation of a subprocess dynamically allocates a command line buffer using `new[]` that is never freed, leaking memory. In practice, this affects Windows nodes using `-signer=<cmd>` whenever an external signer subprocess is executed via RPC or the GUI.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"Popen::execute_process() copied the command line into a buffer from new[], but did not delete it. This leaked memory each time a process started on Windows.\"",
    "PR description notes this was also fixed upstream in arun11299/cpp-subprocess#131."
  ],
